model given the components. A record with \code{1 - h_ii < 1e-8} (a contemporary group or
any fixed level with a single record) has a residual of zero by construction and no
standardization: it is \code{NA}. In \code{\link[=model_ar1]{model_ar1()}} and \code{\link[=model_mt]{model_mt()}} the divisor is
\verb{Var(e) = R0[t, t] - w' C^-1 w}, from the absolute-unit equations.
\item \code{"marginal"}: \verb{y - X b}, which keeps the random effects in.
\item \code{"pearson"}: \verb{e_i sqrt(w_i) / sqrt(s2e)}, the convention of \code{nlme}, NOT standardized
