factorization of the covariance of the OBSERVED cells (a Kalman filter along the
subject's records): the next record is conditioned on what was observed, and only the
missing cells are \code{NA}. As a conditional residual it is computed at the estimates and
carries the same confounding as \code{"conditional"}.
}

The conditional residual is confounded with the random effects (it carries
\verb{R P Z u}; Hilden-Minton 1995, Loy and Hofmann 2015), so a plot of it against the
conditional fitted value \verb{X b + Z u} shows a trend even under the model: compare
against the fixed part \code{fitted(fit, level = "marginal")} instead.

\code{\link[=gibbs]{gibbs()}} returns the posterior mean of the realized residual \verb{y - W loc_s}, which by
linearity is \verb{y - X E[b] - Z E[u]} and shares the same confounding; \code{type = "marginal"}
adds back \verb{Z E[u]}, and \code{fitted()} gives \verb{X E[b] + Z E[u]} or \verb{X E[b]}. For
\code{family = "probit"} the residual is that of the liability (the drawn liability minus
\verb{W loc_s}) and the fitted values are on the liability scale. Only these two types
exist for a chain: it has no leverage, and its residual draws are what
\code{\link[=residual_diagnostics]{residual_diagnostics()}} uses instead.

The threshold and survival methods need the \code{data} again and return plug-in residuals,
computed with the shrunken random effects as if they were known: they are as
